./docs/machine-factory-integration.md:88:| `DART_VERSION` | *(auto)* | Dart SDK for legs on Dart repos (gh-918): hosted runner images ship **no** `dart`, and without it a rework leg cannot run `dart analyze/test/format` or `crap4dart check` to see or verify gate violations. `setup/dart.sh [stable\|beta\|dev\|<version>]` resolves the target the way the repo's own toolchain intent does (gh-1137) — explicit value, else a `.dart-version` pin at the repo root, else the `dart-lang/setup-dart` step's `sdk:`/`channel:` inputs in the repo's own quality workflow, else stable **with a loud warning** that local format/analyzer results may differ from CI. A repo with no `pubspec.yaml` at all skips the install (no SDK is fetched for non-Dart legs). Installs from the same dart-archive CDN under `~/.dart-sdk` and puts it on PATH for the leg session. `DART_VERSION` is a pure input pin: `dart.sh` exports only `DART_HOME`, so a later bare `dart.sh` in the same job still re-resolves (and `setup/cache.sh dart` keys restore/save identically). Dart-repo runners add `bash agents/setup/dart.sh` to `customParams.setupCommands` (self-hosted legs on the engine repo: `bash setup/dart.sh`); the cache key is `DART_CACHE_*` (`setup/cache.sh dart`). `dart.sh summary` (network-free) prints the leg-summary line `toolchain: dart <version> (CI: <pin>, match: yes/no)` — the dev/rework post actions append it to `outputs/response.md` via `js/common/toolchainSummary.js`, so every format/analyzer claim in the summary is checkable against the SDK the leg actually verified with |

