{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: the warning-line pickup is a hidden cross-file string contract**

`fetchToolchainLines` only rides the ⚠️ line along when it starts with `⚠️`, contains the exact substring `differ from CI`, and sits immediately after the `toolchain:` line — all mirroring `cmd_summary`'s wording in `setup/dart.sh`. Nothing ties the two sides together: if the warning in `dart.sh` is ever reworded, `test_dartSetup.js` gets updated to the new phrase, `test_toolchainSummary.js`'s fixture gets updated to match it, and this production filter silently stops matching — the warning just disappears from leg summaries with everything green.

Cheap hardening options:
- Emit a structured marker from `dart.sh summary` (e.g. prefix the warning with `toolchain-warn:` or print it as `toolchain: … warn=<text>` on the same line) and match on that stable token instead of prose;
- or export the phrase as a constant and have at least one test assert the literal string appears in **both** `setup/dart.sh` and `js/common/toolchainSummary.js` (the grep-style wiring-contract pattern this repo already uses in `test_toolchainSummary.js`'s "wiring contracts" suite).
