`fetchToolchainLines` only rides the ⚠️ line along when it starts with `⚠️`, contains the exact substring `differ from CI`, and sits immediately after the `toolchain:` line — all mirroring `cmd_summary`'s wording in `setup/dart.sh`. Nothing ties the two sides together: if the warning in `dart.sh` is ever reworded, `test_dartSetup.js` gets updated to the new phrase, `test_toolchainSummary.js`'s fixture gets updated to match it, and this production filter silently stops matching — the warning just disappears from leg summaries with everything green.

